Resultants -- resultants, discriminants, and Chow forms
*******************************************************

Description
===========

This package provides methods to deal with resultants and discriminants of
multivariate polynomials, and with higher associated subvarieties of
irreducible projective varieties. The main methods are: *note
resultant(Matrix): resultant_lpMatrix_rp,, *note discriminant(RingElement):
discriminant_lpRingElement_rp,, *note chowForm: chowForm,, *note dualVariety:
dualVariety,, and *note tangentialChowForm: tangentialChowForm,. For the
mathematical theory, we refer to the following two books: Using Algebraic
Geometry (see http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2Fb138611 ), by David A.
Cox, John Little, Donal O'shea; Discriminants, Resultants, and Multidimensional
Determinants (see http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-0-8176-4771-1 ),
by Israel M. Gelfand, Mikhail M. Kapranov and Andrei V. Zelevinsky. Other
references for the theory of Chow forms are: The equations defining Chow
varieties (see https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.dmj/1077305197 ), by M. L.
Green and I. Morrison; Multiplicative properties of projectively dual varieties
(see http://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF02567693 ), by J. Weyman and A.
Zelevinsky; and Coisotropic hypersurfaces in Grassmannians (see
https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0747717119301506 ), by
K. Kohn.

