chowEquations -- Chow equations of a projective variety
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        chowEquations W
  * Inputs:
      * W, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the Chow form of
        an irreducible projective variety $X\subset\mathbb{P}^n$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Variable: Grass_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, specify a name for a variable
  * Outputs:
      * the *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, generated by the Chow equations
        of $X$

Description
===========

Given the Chow form $Z_0(X)\subset\mathbb{G}(n-k-1,n)$ of an irreducible
projective $k$-dimensional variety $X\subset\mathbb{P}^n$, one can recover a
canonical system of equations, called Chow equations, that always define $X$
set-theoretically, and also scheme-theoretically whenever $X$ is smooth. For
details, see chapter 3, section 2C of Discriminants, Resultants, and
Multidimensional Determinants (see
http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-0-8176-4771-1 ), by Israel M.
Gelfand, Mikhail M. Kapranov and Andrei V. Zelevinsky.

