chowForm -- Chow form of a projective variety
*********************************************

  * Usage: 
        chowForm I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous ideal defining a
        projective variety $X=V(I)\subset\mathbb{P}^n$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AffineChartGrass: AffineChartGrass, => ..., default value true,
        use an affine chart on the Grassmannian
      * *note AffineChartProj: AffineChartProj, => ..., default value true, use
        an affine chart on the projective space
      * *note Duality: Duality, => ..., default value null, whether to use dual
        Plücker coordinates
      * *note Variable: Grass_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, specify a name for a variable
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the Chow form of $X$
        in the coordinate ring of the Grassmannian
        $\mathbb{G}(n-dim(X)-1,\mathbb{P}^n)$ in the Plücker embedding

