conormalVariety -- conormal variety
***********************************

  * Usage: 
        conormalVariety I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous ideal defining a
        projective variety $X=V(I)\subset\mathbb{P}^n$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note SingularLocus: SingularLocus, => ..., default value null, pass
        the singular locus of the variety
      * *note Strategy: conormalVariety_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value "Saturate",
      * *note Variable: Grass_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, specify a name for a variable
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the bihomogeneous ideal of the
        conormal variety $Con(X)\subset\mathbb{P}^n\times{\mathbb{P}^n}^{*}$ of
        $X$

Description
===========

The conormal variety $Con(X)$ of a projective variety $X\subset\mathbb{P}^n$ is
the Zariski closure in $\mathbb{P}^n\times{\mathbb{P}^n}^{*}$ of the set of
tuples $(x,H)$ where $x$ is a regular point of $X$ and $H$ is a hyperplane in
$\mathbb{P}^n$ containing the embedded tangent space to $X$ at $x$. The dual
variety of $X$ is the image of
$Con(X)\subset\mathbb{P}^n\times{\mathbb{P}^n}^{*}$ under projection onto the
second factor ${\mathbb{P}^n}^{*}$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
