discriminant(RingElement) -- resultant of the partial derivatives
*****************************************************************

  * Function: *note discriminant:
    (Elimination)discriminant_lpRingElement_cmRingElement_rp,
  * Usage: 
        discriminant F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a homogeneous
        polynomial
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Algorithm: resultant_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmAlgorithm=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the discriminant of F

Description
===========

The discriminant of a homogeneous polynomial is defined, up to a scalar factor,
as the *note resultant(Matrix): resultant_lpMatrix_rp, of its partial
derivatives. For the general theory, see one of the following: Using Algebraic
Geometry (see http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2Fb138611 ), by David A.
Cox, John Little, Donal O'shea; Discriminants, Resultants, and Multidimensional
Determinants (see http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-0-8176-4771-1 ),
by Israel M. Gelfand, Mikhail M. Kapranov and Andrei V. Zelevinsky.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : ZZ[a,b,c][x,y]; F = a*x^2+b*x*y+c*y^2             |
|                                                       |
|        2              2                               |
|o2 = a*x  + b*x*y + c*y                                |
|                                                       |
|o2 : ZZ[a..c][x..y]                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : time discriminant F                               |
| -- used 0.0109831s (cpu); 0.0109806s (thread); 0s (gc)|
|                                                       |
|        2                                              |
|o3 = - b  + 4a*c                                       |
|                                                       |
|o3 : ZZ[a..c]                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : ZZ[a,b,c,d][x,y]; F = a*x^3+b*x^2*y+c*x*y^2+d*y^3 |
|                                                       |
|        3      2         2      3                      |
|o5 = a*x  + b*x y + c*x*y  + d*y                       |
|                                                       |
|o5 : ZZ[a..d][x..y]                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : time discriminant F                               |
| -- used 0.0124488s (cpu); 0.0124533s (thread); 0s (gc)|
|                                                       |
|        2 2       3     3                   2 2        |
|o6 = - b c  + 4a*c  + 4b d - 18a*b*c*d + 27a d         |
|                                                       |
|o6 : ZZ[a..d]                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

The next example illustrates how computing the intersection of a pencil
generated by two degree $d$ forms $F(x_0,\ldots,x_n), G(x_0,\ldots,x_n)$ with
the discriminant hypersurface in the space of forms of degree $d$ on
$\mathbb{P}^n$

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
