dualVariety -- projective dual variety
**************************************

  * Usage: 
        dualVariety I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous ideal defining a
        projective variety $X=V(I)\subset\mathbb{P}^n$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AssumeOrdinary: AssumeOrdinary, => ..., default value false,
        whether the expected codimension is 1
      * *note SingularLocus: SingularLocus, => ..., default value null, pass
        the singular locus of the variety
      * *note Strategy: conormalVariety_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value null,
  * Outputs:
      * the *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, of the projective dual variety
        $X^{*}\subset{\mathbb{P}^n}^{*}$

Description
===========

This can be considered a shortcut for dualize tangentialChowForm(I,dim I -1).

Note that in characteristic 0 (or sufficiently large characteristic), the
reflexivity theorem implies that if I' == dualVariety I then dualVariety I' ==
I. Below, we verify the reflexivity theorem for the Veronese surface.

