Grass -- coordinate ring of a Grassmannian
******************************************

  * Usage: 
        Grass(k,n)
        Grass(k,n,K)
  * Inputs:
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * K, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, optional with default value *note
        QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, the coefficient ring to be used
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Variable: Grass_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value "p", specify a name for a variable
  * Outputs:
      * a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, the coordinate ring
        of the Grassmannian variety of all projective $k$-planes in
        $\mathbb{P}^n$

Description
===========

This method calls the method *note Grassmannian: (Macaulay2Doc)Grassmannian,,
and Grass(k,n,K,Variable=>p) can be considered equivalent to quotient
Grassmannian(k,n,Variable=>p,CoefficientRing=>K). However, the method Grass
creates no more than an instance of ring for a given tuple (k,n,K,p).

