Grass(...,Variable=>...) -- specify a name for a variable
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Variable => x

Description
===========

This is an option used to specify a symbol to be used as a name for the
generator of the coordinate ring of the Grassmannian *note Grass: Grass,, or
some other ring.

See also
========

  * *note Grass: Grass, -- coordinate ring of a Grassmannian

Functions with optional argument named Variable:
================================================

  * "GF(...,Variable=>...)" -- see *note GF: (Macaulay2Doc)GF, -- make a finite
    field
  * "cayleyTrick(...,Variable=>...)"
  * "chowEquations(...,Variable=>...)"
  * "chowForm(...,Variable=>...)"
  * "conormalVariety(...,Variable=>...)"
  * "fromPluckerToStiefel(...,Variable=>...)"
  * *note Grass(...,Variable=>...): Grass_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
    -- specify a name for a variable
  * "hurwitzForm(...,Variable=>...)"
  * "plucker(...,Variable=>...)"
  * "tangentialChowForm(...,Variable=>...)"
  * "veronese(...,Variable=>...)"
  * "Grassmannian(...,Variable=>...)" -- see *note Grassmannian:
    (Macaulay2Doc)Grassmannian, -- compute the ideal of the Grassmannian of
    linear subspaces of a vector space
  * normalCone(Ideal,RingElement,Variable=>...) (missing documentation)
  * normalCone(Ideal,Variable=>...) (missing documentation)
  * "Schubert(...,Variable=>...)" -- see *note Schubert:
    (Macaulay2Doc)Schubert, -- compute the Plücker ideal of a Schubert variety

Further information
===================

  * Default value: p
  * Function: *note Grass: Grass, -- coordinate ring of a Grassmannian
  * Option key: *note Variable: (Macaulay2Doc)Variable, -- an optional argument
