isInCoisotropic -- test membership in a coisotropic hypersurface
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isInCoisotropic(L,I)
  * Inputs:
      * L, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the ideal of a $k$-dimensional
        linear subspace $V(L)\subset\mathbb{P}^n$, which corresponds to a point
        $p_L\in\mathbb{G}(k,\mathbb{P}^n)$
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the ideal of a $d$-dimensional
        projective variety $X=V(I)\subset\mathbb{P}^n$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Duality: Duality, => ..., default value null, whether to use dual
        Plücker coordinates
      * *note SingularLocus: SingularLocus, => ..., default value null, pass
        the singular locus of the variety
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $p_L$ belongs to
        the $s$-th associated subvariety
        $Z_s(X)\subset\mathbb{G}(k,\mathbb{P}^n)$ with $s = k+d+1-n$

Description
===========

This is equivalent to isSubset(ideal tangentialChowForm(I,s),plucker L), but it
