resultant(...,Algorithm=>...)
*****************************

  * Usage: 
        Algorithm => "Poisson"/"Macaulay"/"Poisson2"/"Macaulay2"

Description
===========

This is an option that determines which algorithm will be used to compute the
*note resultant: (Elimination)resultant_lpRingElement_cmRingElement_
cmRingElement_rp,. There are currently four algorithms implemented:

"Poisson" (default) the resultant is computed, recursively, through the Poisson
Formula (see [1, Theorem 3.4]);

"Macaulay" the resultant is computed as a Macaulay resultant, i.e. as a ratio
of two determinants (see [1, Theorem 4.9]);

"Poisson2" and "Macaulay2" these are variants of the above ones using
interpolation of multivariate polynomials.

[1] David A. Cox, John Little, Donal O'shea - Using Algebraic Geometry (see
http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2Fb138611 ), Graduate Texts in
Mathematics, Volume 185 (2005).

