resultant(Matrix) -- multipolynomial resultant
**********************************************

  * Function: *note resultant:
    (Elimination)resultant_lpRingElement_cmRingElement_cmRingElement_rp,
  * Usage: 
        resultant F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a row matrix whose entries
        are $n+1$ homogeneous polynomials $F_0,\ldots,F_n$ in $n+1$ variables
        (or a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, to be interpreted as such a
        matrix)
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Algorithm: resultant_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmAlgorithm=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the resultant of
        $F_0,\ldots,F_n$

Description
===========

Let $F_0,\ldots,F_n$ be $n+1$ homogeneous polynomials in $n+1$ variables
$x_0,\ldots,x_n$ over a commutative ring $K$. The resultant $R(F_0,\ldots,F_n)$
is a certain polynomial in the coefficients of $F_0,\ldots,F_n$; when $K$ is an
algebraically closed field, $R(F_0,\ldots,F_n)$ vanishes if and only if
$F_0,\ldots,F_n$ have a common nontrivial root.  For the general theory, see
one of the following: Using Algebraic Geometry (see
http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2Fb138611 ), by David A. Cox, John
Little, Donal O'shea; Discriminants, Resultants, and Multidimensional
Determinants (see http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-0-8176-4771-1 ),
by Israel M. Gelfand, Mikhail M. Kapranov and Andrei V. Zelevinsky.

