SingularLocus -- pass the singular locus of the variety
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        SingularLocus => X

Description
===========

Some methods, like *note tangentialChowForm: tangentialChowForm, and *note
conormalVariety: conormalVariety,, must calculate the singular locus of the
input variety, which can be hard to obtain. Sometimes one knows this locus and
this option allows to inform Macaulay2.

Functions with optional argument named SingularLocus:
=====================================================

  * "conormalVariety(...,SingularLocus=>...)"
  * "dualVariety(...,SingularLocus=>...)"
  * "hurwitzForm(...,SingularLocus=>...)"
  * "isInCoisotropic(...,SingularLocus=>...)"
  * "tangentialChowForm(...,SingularLocus=>...)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note SingularLocus: SingularLocus, is a *note symbol:
(Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

