veronese -- Veronese embedding
******************************

  * Usage: 
        veronese(n,d,K) 
        veronese(n,d)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * K, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, optional, with default value
        *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Variable: Grass_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, specify a name for a variable
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, representing the $d$-th
        Veronese embedding of $\mathbb{P}^n$

Description
===========

This is an auxiliary method to build tests and examples. For instance, the two
following codes have to produce the same polynomial up to a renaming of
variables: 1) resultant genericPolynomials((n+1):d,K) and 2)
fromPluckerToStiefel dualize chowForm veronese(n,d,K).

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : veronese(1,4)                                                 |
|                                                                   |
|                                    4   3     2 2     3   4        |
|o1 = map (QQ[t ..t ], QQ[x ..x ], {t , t t , t t , t t , t })      |
|              0   1       0   4     0   0 1   0 1   0 1   1        |
|                                                                   |
|o1 : RingMap QQ[t ..t ] <-- QQ[x ..x ]                             |
|                 0   1          0   4                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : veronese(1,4,Variable=>y)                                     |
|                                                                   |
|                                    4   3     2 2     3   4        |
|o2 = map (QQ[y ..y ], QQ[y ..y ], {y , y y , y y , y y , y })      |
|              0   1       0   4     0   0 1   0 1   0 1   1        |
|                                                                   |
|o2 : RingMap QQ[y ..y ] <-- QQ[y ..y ]                             |
|                 0   1          0   4                              |
